  "title": "Kirby Problem 4.24",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let K be a framed knot in $S^{3} = \\partial B^{4}$. Let U be a meridian of K. Does there exist a smoothly embedded disk D in $B^{4} \\cup _{\\nu K} h^{2}$ bounded by U that intersects the cocore of $h^{2}$ algebraically zero times, such that the 4-manifold obtained by removing an open tubular neighborhood of the disk is not diffeomorphic to the 4-ball?",
